    "body": "## What\n\nTwo related pieces:\n\n### 1. Cost display: billed cost, cached tokens, and cache savings\n\nSurfaces the caching/cost data dev already records (per-request OpenRouter `cost`, cache read/write tokens) in the UI:\n\n- **`/cost`** now shows **Billed** (actual OpenRouter charge), **cached tokens**, and **Saved** (list price \u2212 billed), alongside the existing list-price estimate.\n- **Per-message expanded usage rows**: \"Cached this turn\", \"Saved by caching\", and the exact per-token input price used \u2014 numbers are auditable, not trust-us.\n- **Fixes input-token inflation**: OpenRouter folds the cache write into `prompt_tokens` on cache-write turns, so raw sums read ~2\u00d7 high. Session totals and the per-message meter now subtract `cache_write_tokens`.\n\n### 2. Prompt-caching eval suite (`agent-docs/caching-eval/`)\n\n- **`./hazel agent-eval`** (new CLI subcommand): drives the **real `Agent.Update` loop headless** against live OpenRouter \u2014 real system prompt + dev notes cache anchor, real tools/tool execution, real payload serialization and usage parsing \u2014 via a synchronous curl-backed XHR polyfill in `src/CLI/polyfill.js`. Simulates a user session with scripted inputs.\n- **`harness/run_eval.mjs`**: provider-isolated JS control harness (byte-mirrors the wire shape, no app code) with a free `--dry-run` cost estimator.\n- Append-only JSONL data accumulators (raw requests/responses, per-turn results, verdicts, `/credits` ledger) + pre-implementation report + findings.\n\n### Findings from the full 4-model run (2026-08-04)\n\n| model | caching | note |\n|---|---|---|\n| claude-haiku-4.5 | \u2705 working | turn-2 cost \u221287% |\n| claude-sonnet-4.6 | \u2705 working | session saved $1.16 vs list |\n| gemini-3-flash-preview | \u2705 working | confirms the `prompt_tokens` double-report this PR corrects |\n| qwen/qwen3-coder | \u274c **not caching at all** | billed ~4\u00d7 Haiku for an equivalent session |\n\nThe eval also exercised this PR's `cost_payload` accumulator live \u2014 billed/cached/saved came out coherent, and the \"saved\" line correctly vanishes where nothing was saved.\n\n## Testing\n\n- Full suite passes (3296 tests), clean build (including the new CLI target).\n- Live validation: real headless agent sessions across 4 models (data committed under `agent-docs/caching-eval/outputs/`), `/cost` cross-checked against raw provider usage.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_0114p9PxJUoXZpeUdVGzQ7A2",
